# Agent Run DOCX Reports (mandatory)

## Requirement

Whenever a named agent completes (or stops with Blocked/Incomplete), produce a **Word document** summarizing what was done at a high level. Store under:

`docs/agent-runs/<agent-slug>/`

See `docs/agent-runs/README.md` for layout and payload examples.

## How to generate

1. **Auto-hook runners** (DOCX written automatically):
   - `defect-regression` → `pipeline/scripts/defect-regression-run.js`
   - `execute-raise-defects` / `qa:run-module` → `pipeline/scripts/execute-raise-defects.js`
   - **Milestone module runs** (`milestone:run`, direct `playwright test` under `tests/milestoneN/`) → `pipeline/scripts/finalize-module-run.cjs` via `pipeline-reporter.ts`
   - `qa-automation-pipeline` → `pipeline/scripts/verify-qa-pipeline-completion.cjs`
   - `fsd-figma-pipeline` → `pipeline/scripts/render-stage0-coverage-report.cjs`
   - `fsd-excel-coverage-audit` → `pipeline/scripts/render-coverage-audit-report.cjs`

2. **One-command npm scripts** (MCP agents — run at end of agent turn):
   - `npm run docs:agent-run:generator -- --results-root "<path>" --batch <N>`
   - `npm run docs:agent-run:healer -- --results-root "<path>" --batch <N>`

3. **Generic CLI** (custom payload or artifact flags):

   `npm run docs:agent-run -- --agent <slug> [--payload json | --gate | --results-key | --plan | ...]`

4. **Programmatic:** `require("./write-agent-run-docx.cjs").writeAgentRunReport(agent, payload, artifactOptions)`

## Minimum content by agent type

| Agent | Must document |
|-------|----------------|
| defect-regression | Resolved defects picked (TC ID + description from Google), regression cases executed, Closed/Reopened/unchanged counts |
| execute-raise-defects | Spec scope, pass/fail, failed TC IDs + descriptions, local defect files, Google sync status |
| qa-automation-pipeline | Excel path, batch pass/fail per batch, live UI coverage %, gate result, remaining failures |
| fsd-figma-pipeline | FSD/Figma sources, coverage %, feature delta, TC delta, Excel path |
| fsd-excel-coverage-audit | Audit verdict, audit vs writer coverage %, **feature-wise Actual/Req/Flow/UC %**, per-feature gaps, orphan TCs |
| test-generator / healer | Cases in scope, live routes validated, files changed, pass/fail or heal outcomes |

Use agent-specific formatters when registered; otherwise use the generic payload (`highlights`, `overview`, `sections`).

## Failure behavior

- DOCX failure → status **Incomplete** for documentation; include CLI error in the reply
- Do not skip DOCX because JSON artifacts already exist — the DOCX is the stakeholder-facing record
- Record `agentRunDocx` on summary JSON when auto-hooks succeed

## Do not

- Store agent run DOCX outside `docs/agent-runs/`
- Fabricate counts or case lists not backed by execution/summary artifacts
- Omit the DOCX path from the final user message when generation succeeded
